From 10bc78dbc43125c8b5736e8ac4653f49815b5d43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:53:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [M150] media: Enforce baseline symbol limit for DC Huffman
 tables in JPEG parser

Original change's description:
> media: Enforce baseline symbol limit for DC Huffman tables in JPEG parser
>
> According to the ITU-T T.81 baseline JPEG specification, DC difference
> coding supports at most 12 symbols (categories 0..11), whereas AC
> coefficients support up to 162 symbols.
>
> The JPEG parser previously applied the AC limit (162) to both table
> classes in DHT segments. This allowed malformed bitstreams with DC code
> lengths summing to >12 to be passed to hardware decoders like VA-API,
> where the driver struct VAHuffmanTableBufferJPEGBaseline allocates only
> 12 entries for dc_values.
>
> This CL enforces a maximum of 12 symbols for DC tables in parse_jpeg.rs
> and adds unit tests verifying DC and AC symbol boundaries.
>
